The  command produces output similar to but for the list of hosts
or all machines on the local network.  For each  host  responding
to  the  rusers  query,  the hostname with the names of the users
currently logged on is printed on each line.  The rusers  command
will wait for one minute to catch late responders.  The following
options  are  available: Print all machines responding even if no
one is currently logged in.  Print a long format  listing.   This
includes the user name, host name, tty that the user is logged in
to,  the date and time the user logged in, the idle time (in min‐
utes), and the remote host they logged in from  (if  applicable).
